# Review package: ticket 06, f8ed18d..ee865c1

## Commits
### ee865c1
docs(core): record the performance gate report for ticket 06

Ticket 06 asks for the full benchmark output of every attempt, the
percentages against ticket 01 and the check results on the final commit,
94ffb56, in the ticket report.

### 94ffb56
perf(state): look the wrapper up in the method cache before the name check

A wrapped method is read far more often than it is first wrapped, so the
get handler now returns on the cache hit after the array and function
checks, instead of paying the name check and a call on every read.

### 54823b6
perf(state): cut allocation and batch overhead on the array method path

The array method wrapper allocated a batch closure per call, and the
batch fast path allocated a Set per batch for the array target although
flushDirtyTargets ignores the recorded properties of an array. Heap per
benchmark sample of the array cases tripled against ticket 01.

Map a dirty array to a shared sentinel set, look subscribers up only on
a target's first write of the batch, run the batch bookkeeping in the
wrapper through the new abortBatch and endBatch helpers that batch()
now shares, and skip the deferred effect pass when nothing was deferred.


